From: sadatdaniel <sadatdaniel@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] security: preserve the default hook result after integrity checks

Samsung's integrity check overwrites RC even when no LSM implements the
requested hook. With AppArmor active, secid_to_secctx has no implementation
in this tree: it falsely returns success instead of -EOPNOTSUPP, leaving
SCM_SECURITY's context pointer and length unset. On the A50, journald then
panics the kernel in hardened usercopy while receiving a Unix datagram.

Restore the caller's default after a successful integrity check, as the
upstream dispatcher preserves it for an empty hook list. Integrity failures
and installed hooks retain their existing behavior. Do not weaken usercopy.

Test: build/test-security-hook-default.py fails for the original dispatcher
and passes after this change. Device boot validation remains pending.

---
--- a/security/security.c
+++ b/security/security.c
@@ -217,6 +217,7 @@
 		RC = security_integrity_current();		\
 		if (RC != 0)							\
 			break;								\
+		RC = IRC;					\
 		list_for_each_entry(P, &security_hook_heads.FUNC, list) { \
 			RC = P->hook.FUNC(__VA_ARGS__);		\
 			if (RC != 0)				\
